This code sets up a Raspberry Pi to monitor three PIR motion sensors on GPIO pins 17, 27, and 22, and a VL53L0X Time-of-Flight sensor on the I2C bus. When motion is detected on any PIR sensor, it reads the distance from the ToF sensor and validates the occupancy. If the distance is below 1.0 meter, it logs the event to a file. The code also handles errors and exceptions, and registers a signal handler to clean up resources when the program exits.

