This code implements a parking sensor system using two HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensors connected to the Raspberry Pi's GPIO pins. The system calibrates the sensors against a known distance and then continuously measures the distance between the sensors and the car. The system uses a simple moving-average filter to smooth out the distance readings and applies three thresholds to determine the actuator activation. The system logs all events with timestamps to a file named `parking_sensor.log`. The system runs both sensors concurrently using threads and handles SIGINT/SIGTERM cleanly by releasing all GPIO resources.

